# Handoff Packet Rule

All cross-role handoffs must use a complete packet. Missing fields means INVALID-HANDOFF.

Required fields:
- `work_item_id`
- `from_role`
- `to_role`
- `entry_criteria`
- `exit_criteria`
- `evidence_path`
- `needed_by`
- `ack_status`
- `pm_dispatch_hint` (optional — Dev/QA gợi ý work_item P0 cho PM; template `.cursor/templates/ROLE_DISPATCH_PROMPT.md`)
- `completion_report` (required — nêu phần đã đóng + residual)
- `next_owner` (required)
- `next_dispatch_prompt` (required — copy-ready prompt để PM dispatch ngay)

Execution policy:
- PM dispatch must include owner, deadline window, and next reviewer.
- Dev-BE Lead handoff to FE/Mobile must include API contract notes and version impact.
- QA handoff to QC must include defect status and test evidence.
- QC Go/No-Go must reference concrete evidence paths.

Acceptance policy:
- No DONE status without evidence and traceability mapping.
- Any ambiguity must be escalated to PM and logged to the project decisions log.
- Confirm-only completion without `next_dispatch_prompt` is INVALID-HANDOFF.
